# Build context hygiene. Everything here is either irrelevant to the runtime
# image or actively unwanted in it.

# Rebuilt inside the image
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# The API imports ml/ for the review queue (backend/review.py), so the library
# itself ships. Its heavy imports are lazy, so this adds no dependency to
# backend/requirements.txt — the cold-start prior is pure Python.
#
# Two things are excluded on purpose:
#
#  - ml/artifacts/ is the ASSISTments checkpoint. Its skill ids are that
#    dataset's, not any Marigold user's, so `concept_to_skill` is empty and the
#    SAKT path returns nothing regardless. Shipping it would make the loader
#    import PyTorch at first request — ~2GB in the image — to produce exactly
#    the prior-path answers it produces without it. It belongs here once a model
#    is trained on Marigold's own data, together with torch in requirements.
#  - ml/data/ is the training corpus and its loaders; nothing at request time
#    reads them.
ml/artifacts/
ml/data/raw/
ml/training/
ml/tests/
.github/
.git/
# Agent worktrees: a second checkout of this repo, hundreds of megabytes of
# build context that would be uploaded on every build and used by nothing.
.claude/

# Tests do not ship
backend/tests/
.pytest_cache
pytest.ini

# Local artefacts
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
backend/*.db
*.db
.env
.venv
venv/
